 "fn-77": "<a href=\"https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/小塚原刑場\"><code>kozukappara-jawiki</code></a> - 「In the Edo period there was the Kozukappara execution ground to the north and, to the south, the Suzugamori execution ground along the Tokaido (Minami-Oi, Shinagawa ward, Tokyo), and they were called the two great execution grounds.」 (translated from the Japanese by this project; original: 「江戸時代は北に小塚原刑場、南に東海道沿いの鈴ヶ森刑場（東京都品川区南大井）があり、二大刑場といわれた。」) (as above.)",
 "fn-78": "<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Susquehanna_Boom\"><code>susquehanna-boom</code></a> - \"These cribs built of local mountain stone and sunken timber were stretched diagonally across the river, beginning on the south side near Duboistown and ending on the north side near Linden.\"",
